  "step_3": "The decision reason applies to this problem and favors Lottery B because it lacks a sure outcome, while A has one. The individual also recognizes that A involves a certain loss and values that B offers a chance (20%) to avoid any loss. Their reasoning emphasizes the contrast between the certainty of loss in A and the uncertainty in B, particularly the possibility of a zero loss. This aligns with sensitivity to the presence of a sure outcome, which is the core of the decision reason. Although the individual does not explicitly state they prefer 'not having a sure outcome', their emphasis on the value of a chance to avoid loss indicates they are influenced by the same structural feature—the presence or absence of certainty. The reasoning is consistent with the decision reason, even if not articulated in identical terms.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
