  "step_3": "The decision reason hinges on detecting whether a lottery has a sure outcome (100% probability) and prefers the one without it. However, in this case, *neither* lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would not clearly prefer one over the other based on its rule. The individual, meanwhile, bases their reasoning on the high probability of loss in Lottery A (90% chance of losing 3000 Euros), which reflects a sensitivity to the magnitude and likelihood of losses, not to the presence of sure outcomes. There is no mention or implication that the individual checked whether any outcome was certain in either lottery. The information considered (high loss probability in A) is unrelated to the structural feature (sure outcome) that the decision reason evaluates. Furthermore, the justification (avoiding high chance of loss) differs from the reason’s rule (prefer lottery without sure outcome). Since the relevant information and the decision rule are both absent from the verbal report, it is unlikely the individual used this reason.",
